  // Lightkeeper access line: To the Light - Getting Acquainted and the Make
  // Amends re-entry chain. tarkov.dev served all ten of these IDs until early
  // October 2026, then dropped them from regular, pve and pvp-season task data
  // (upstream regression: https://github.com/the-hideout/tarkov-data-manager/issues/886).
  // Each definition below is tarkov.dev's own regular-mode data as archived at
  // https://web.archive.org/web/20261004024103/https://json.tarkov.dev/regular/tasks
  // (names from .../regular/tasks_en), reshaped to this schema. Every task,
  // objective, item, map and trader ID is upstream's; nothing is synthesized.
  // The wiki pages linked per entry are current (no {{Historical content}}).
  // Remove these once tarkov.dev serves the IDs again (check-overrides flags it).
  //
  // Getting Acquainted keeps upstream's only start edge (Knock-Knock,
  // 625d7005a4eb80027c4f2e09) even though that task is retired; it is re-added
  // below as a disabled anchor. The wiki reads Getting Acquainted as following
  // "To the Light - The Other Side", but that quest has no known ID and the wiki
  // `previous` field is not proof of an unlock edge (AGENTS.md), so the recorded
  // edge is kept and consumers resolve it as unknown rather than available.
  //
  // Upstream names all three Make Amends hand-ins (6391d90f..., 6391d912...,
  // 6391d914...) just "Make Amends" and they share objective IDs; the
  // "(after <task>)" suffix is an overlay label so each ID keeps a unique name.
  // The other ten "To the Light - ..." quests (Trust but Verify through The Other
  // Side) have no known task or objective IDs; they are added below as
  // placeholders (see the placeholder block at the end of this file).

  // To the Light - Getting Acquainted
  // Proof: https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/To_the_Light_-_Getting_Acquainted
